Check that we didn't miss any needed predicates like candidate_origin_availability_linked etc are present from init and not removed.

We also need to ensure that after we detach task profile from origin/destination, we still have candidate_origin_availability_linked etc (unchanged). Good.

Now we need to verify that we didn't violate any precondition like (not (candidate_created ?candidate)) when we create again; we only create each once.

Now check that we didn't accidentally try to allocate vehicle to a candidate that already has vehicle allocated (we allocate only once per candidate before dispatch). After dispatch, we do not deallocate vehicle; but we don't try to allocate again to same candidate.

Now check that we didn't try to assign operator to a candidate that already has operator linked (we release before reassigning). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to assign skill certificate to a candidate that already has it linked (we release before reassigning). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to assign compliance certificate to a candidate that already has it linked (we release before reassigning). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to apply operational constraint to a candidate that already has constraint_applied (we apply only once per candidate). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to confirm operator alignment before constraint applied (we do after apply). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to verify compliance certificate before operator_alignment_confirmed (we do after). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to finalize before compliance_validation_complete (we do after verify). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to allocate dispatch slot before dispatch_ready (we allocate after finalize which sets dispatch_ready). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to execute dispatch before dispatch_allocated (we allocate then execute). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to detach task profile when it's not linked (we detach after we attached and before we need it again; we ensure it's linked). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to attach task profile when it's not available (we detach before each attach). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to activate origin node before candidate_prepared and task profile linked (we have). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to lock origin availability before candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, origin_node_ready, not origin_availability_locked. We have candidate_prepared true (step4), candidate_operator_linked true (step5), origin_node_ready true (step6), origin_availability_locked false (we haven't locked yet). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to lock destination similarly.

Now check that we didn't try to assemble transport leg before origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available. We have all after steps7,8,15,16,6,14,7,15, and transport_leg_available init. Good.

Now check that we didn't try to authorize transport leg loading before transport_leg_assembled and origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked (we attached origin's task profile before authorize). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to mark dispatch ready before transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized (we have). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to allocate dispatch slot before dispatch_ready (we have after mark). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to execute dispatch before dispatch_allocated (we have after allocate). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to release operator before we assigned it (we release after assign). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to release skill certificate before assigning (we release after assign). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to release compliance certificate before assigning (we release after assign). Good.

Now check that we didn't try to detach task profile when it's not linked (we detach after we attached and before we need it again; we ensure it's linked). Good